            "body": "> Is this more general than as documented here? I think I've hit this with `r` when my cursor is directly above another cursor, and follow mode is off. Was planning on making a minimal repro.\n\nMaybe. I can reproduce the issue described here, although its behavior is slightly more reasonable than in this issue. It is documented that `Normal-mode commands, Mappings, and even Macros (|@|) replay at each cursor.`, which (apparently) means both extra and main cursor. The `r` seems to move the extmark for the extra cursor to the right and then cascade edit to it.\nAlthough I'd probably expect edits on duplicated cursors to be done only once, yeah.",
