            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "@justinmk, the repro from the first comment is indeed solved, but the culprit doesn't look like 100% resolved:\n\n- The `r` case is indeed not resolved and is a bit counter-intuitive. Doing `vip` - `Q` - `rx` does more than it should.\n- Operators still get applied twice if the main cursor is on one of the extra cursors. Both immediately after `vip` - `Q` and if the main cursor is on top of existing cursor. The minimal repro with two lines `aa` and `bb` in paragraph: `vip` - `Q` - `g~~`. It inverts the case of the first line, but doesn't (because applied twice) on the second.",
